      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/venetian_village_illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before settlers arrived, the Potawatomi, Ottawa, and Chippewa tribes called the area home in the early 1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/venetian_village_illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Glacial activity carved Venetian Village’s lakes, linking them into the Chain O'Lakes system that shapes local property layouts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/venetian_village_illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "What began as summer retreats evolved into a quiet suburb, still offering a vacation‑like ambiance within 50 miles of Chicago.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
